{"kind":"assert","text":"Asking for a widening rather than taking it, per this request's own last clause.\n\nCODEX'S VERDICT fd14cec7 on head 128132f2 is ratified at my hand. Two blockers. One is mine to fix inside this scope; the other is not, and that is what I am asking about.\n\nINSIDE SCOPE, and I will do it without further authorization. Artifacts ad10ba6c at docs/reference/gs/serve.md and 4b2335ac at docs/reference/architecture.md describe cmd/gs behaviour but do not rest on 9936cbb2, the cmd/gs artifact at the same head. They were published before your ruling 0139dd87 existed, so the cmd/gs artifact they should have named had not been filed yet. Documentation that describes behaviour must rest on the artifacts for that behaviour, or it can never flare when that behaviour moves. Both paths are already in this request's set, so republishing them with complete bases needs nothing new from you.\n\nOUTSIDE SCOPE, and this is the ask. internal/app/resident.go carries a comment saying a dead resident makes every durable write refuse, and an untrusted advertisement refuses every caller. Both sentences were true of the world before this head and are false of the world after it: the adapter now permits a read to answer locally, and permits a local degraded fold after transport loss through a record that still reads. internal/app is not one of the six paths this request names, and correcting a comment there changes a file outside the authorized diff — which would then need its own artifact, and would move the head.\n\nWHY I THINK IT SHOULD BE WIDENED RATHER THAN DEFERRED. The comment is the in-code statement of exactly the security boundary this lane exists to correct. Leaving it means the repository asserts the old contract in the file that owns the classification, while three documentation pages assert the new one. That is the same defect the head is fixing, one layer down, and a follow-up row for a two-sentence comment costs more ceremony than the fix.\n\nONE MORE THING I WOULD FOLD IN IF YOU WIDEN. Codex's simplification note asks to narrow the serve.md transport-loss prose: a rewrite landing mid-call refuses the local fallback only when the re-read is untrusted, while removal or a valid replacement may still fall back. My wording overstates it. serve.md is already in scope, but the change moves the head, so it may as well land with the comment correction rather than in a third round.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING MEANWHILE. Not republishing the two artifacts yet. If you widen, the head moves and every artifact is republished at the new head anyway, so filing corrected bases now would produce one round of supersessions I would immediately supersede again. If you decline the widening, say so and I will republish the two at this head and refile the review request the same hour."}